TITLE:: AmpCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that sets amplitude on selected piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::AmpCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::amp:: that writes amplitude onto selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::values:: is a space-separated list of LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::s. Notes are ordered by CODE::startTime:: only. Notes that share a start time take the same array value; the list wraps and advances only when start time changes. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: are clipped silently. Each note stores the clipped value in its composed LINK::Classes/Event:: as CODE::\amp:: and maps it to MIDI velocity with CODE::linlin(0, 1, 0, 127)::.

Example: five notes at beats CODE::0, 1, 1, 2, 3:: with CODE::amp values 1 0.5:: become amps CODE::1, 0.5, 0.5, 1, 0.5::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::AmpCommand::. Takes no arguments; amplitude is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::AmpCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Applies wrapped, clipped amplitude values to CODE::\selectedNotes:: grouped by start time.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::amp_::) and CODE::\values:: (a non-empty LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::s).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var notes = 5.collect({
	|i|
	var note = PianoRollNote(i, 60, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		setPart1Func: {},
		setPart2Func: {},
		setPart3Func: {},
		setPart4Func: {},
		moveFunc: {}
	);
	note.stop(i + 1.0);
	note;
});
AmpCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: notes,
	values: [1, 0.5]
));
)
::
